[2.265, "o", "OpenMathInstruct-2 train_1M: 950,000 training / 50,000 held-out problems\r\nFirst training prompt, as the model sees it (before the chat template):\r\n  │ Think step-by-step to solve the following problem. Output your answer inside of \\\\boxed{} tags.:\r\n  │ An octahedron has eight equilateral triangular faces, each with side length 1. Let $P$ be a point inside\r\n  │ the octahedron, and let $d_1, d_2, \\ldots, d_8$ be the distances from $P$ to the centroids of the eight\r\n  │ faces of the octahedron. Find the largest possible value of the sum $d_1 + d_2 + \\cdots + d_8$.\r\n  │\r\n  │ Let's think step-by-step\r\n  expected answer: \\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}  (the reward is 1 when the \\boxed{} answer matches)\r\n"]
